comments[4]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-08-03T18:14:18.504Z","harness:codex","Duplicate check: exact advisory-id searches across all pm statuses returned zero items. Broader package searches found only closed predecessor advisories pm-5q81jq, pm-f5hy2n, and pm-a24aqt for different GHSAs; this item preserves new advisory lineage instead of reopening completed fixes."
  "2026-08-03T18:40:17.025Z","harness:codex","Security evidence: pnpm audit initially reported high GHSA-rgw5-rvv9-x895 through brace-expansion 5.0.8 and moderate GHSA-fxqj-rqcc-2cmp through postcss 8.5.22 while GitHub Dependabot/code-scanning/secret-scanning APIs each reported zero open alerts. Overrides now require brace-expansion >=5.0.9 <6 and postcss >=8.5.23 <9; the resolved graph uses patched versions and pnpm audit reports no known vulnerabilities. tsx was refreshed to 4.23.5."
  "2026-08-03T19:30:45.061Z","harness:codex","Exact-head PR evidence (PR #884, c361624e2): every hosted required check passes, including static/typecheck/coverage/smokes/compat, Ubuntu/macOS/Windows runtime smoke, benchmarks, CodeQL, Semgrep, Trivy, TruffleHog, DeepScan, CodeFactor, Codecov, ShellCheck, PSScriptAnalyzer, actionlint, and Docs/Skills. The complete sandboxed local suite passes 428 files / 6,792 tests at exact 100% statements, branches, functions, and lines; lint, zero-clone analysis, 100% docstring gates, contracts, and focused review regressions pass. All 12 CodeRabbit threads were individually replied to and reacted to; nine actionable findings were fixed in c361624e2 and all threads are resolved. The requested exact-head CodeRabbit rerun was included-review-rate-limited and the authenticated Greptile gate returned free_reviews_limit_reached; these are reviewer limitations, not clean-review claims."
  "2026-08-03T19:40:16.425Z","harness:codex","Merge and operational evidence: PR #884 merged to main as 657f8fa56a1e56c918095a58600c49188206e180; local main equals origin/main and the worktree is clean. No open PRs remain; GitHub Dependabot, code-scanning, and secret-scanning each report zero open alerts; pnpm audit reports no known vulnerabilities. Telemetry flush at 2026-08-03T19:36:53.267Z successfully drained four queued events, while subsequent status commands generated fresh self-observability rows. Live Sentry 14-day data shows no new issue attributable to this tranche; older unresolved PM-CLI-2S and PM-CLI-2Q remain independently tracked by open pm-4odf0c and pm-qyg51h. The sole immutable same-day tag/package remains v2026.8.3 / @unbrained/pm-cli@2026.8.3; the scheduled Auto Release already proved same-day no-op behavior after that release, so this post-tag merge is intentionally eligible for the next UTC daily release rather than creating or moving a duplicate same-day version."
notes[1]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-08-03T18:40:17.470Z","harness:codex","Compatibility boundary: npm-package-arg 14 is intentionally deferred because its Node engine excludes the supported Node 22.18 floor. TypeScript 7 is intentionally deferred because typescript-eslint 8.66 supports TypeScript below 6.1. These are incompatible majors rather than unattended safe updates."
learnings[1]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-08-03T18:40:17.932Z","harness:codex",GitHub alert APIs can be clean while a newly published advisory is already visible to the package-manager audit. Release readiness needs both remote alert inventories and a fresh lockfile-native audit with explicit secure override floors.
